From: Prævit <software@praevit.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Export functions for DXMT.

DXMT (Metal-based Direct3D 10/11) finds the Mac driver's window and Metal
view functions with dlsym() through a "macdrv_functions" table. winemac.so
hides its symbols and its macdrv_win_data no longer has the layout DXMT
expects, so export a table with a get_win_data that returns that layout.

diff --color -ruN a/dlls/winemac.drv/Makefile.in b/dlls/winemac.drv/Makefile.in
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/Makefile.in
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 	cocoa_window.m \
 	display.c \
 	dllmain.c \
+	dxmt.c \
 	event.c \
 	gdi.c \
 	image.c \
diff --color -ruN a/dlls/winemac.drv/dxmt.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/dxmt.c
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/dxmt.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/dxmt.c
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+/*
